From: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+alilinux@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:32:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mips nommu: /dev/mem mmap hands out the KSEG1 view
 (busybox devmem)

Without an MMU the address get_unmapped_area_mem() returns is used as the
user pointer.  On nommu MIPS userland runs in kernel mode on the fixed
mapping, where a physical address is not a usable pointer: return its
uncached KSEG1 alias and accept it in the nommu remap_pfn_range().
Both functions exist only without an MMU; other architectures unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/char/mem.c | 7 +++++++
 mm/nommu.c         | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/char/mem.c b/drivers/char/mem.c
index 6ebe2b86..12429b92 100644
--- a/drivers/char/mem.c
+++ b/drivers/char/mem.c
@@ -314,4 +314,11 @@ static unsigned long get_unmapped_area_mem(struct file *file,
 	if (!valid_mmap_phys_addr_range(pgoff, len))
 		return (unsigned long) -EINVAL;
+#ifdef CONFIG_MIPS
+	/* nommu MIPS: hand out the uncached KSEG1 view (registers, devmem);
+	 * KSEG1 covers the low 512 MB only, CKSEG1ADDR() would wrap above it */
+	if (((pgoff << PAGE_SHIFT) + len) > 0x20000000UL || (pgoff << PAGE_SHIFT) > 0x20000000UL)
+		return (unsigned long) -EINVAL;
+	return CKSEG1ADDR(pgoff << PAGE_SHIFT);
+#endif
 	return pgoff << PAGE_SHIFT;
 }
diff --git a/mm/nommu.c b/mm/nommu.c
index b2adb43e..c81359e4 100644
--- a/mm/nommu.c
+++ b/mm/nommu.c
@@ -1780,4 +1780,9 @@ int remap_pfn_range(struct vm_area_struct *vma, unsigned long addr,
 		unsigned long pfn, unsigned long size, pgprot_t prot)
 {
+#ifdef CONFIG_MIPS
+	/* the KSEG1 view handed out by /dev/mem (drivers/char/mem.c) */
+	if (addr == CKSEG1ADDR(pfn << PAGE_SHIFT))
+		addr = pfn << PAGE_SHIFT;
+#endif
 	if (addr != (pfn << PAGE_SHIFT))
 		return -EINVAL;
